===Motivation===

[https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0327.mediawiki BIP327] specifies MuSig2, an ''n''-of-''n'' multi-signature protocol that supports non-interactive public-key aggregation and allows multiple signers to cooperatively produce an ordinary [https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0340.mediawiki BIP340] Schnorr signature under the resulting aggregate public key. MuSig2 signing consists of two communication rounds; signers first provide public nonces and subsequently provide partial signatures.

[https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0327.mediawiki BIP327] treats the participant public keys as a single, flat key-aggregation set. In some protocols, however, a logical participant may itself be represented by a MuSig2 signing group. Replacing such a group by all of its individual participant keys at the outer aggregation level removes the distinction between the subgroup and the outer signing group. In particular, the subgroup's participant keys become part of the outer key-aggregation set and the outer signing protocol must coordinate with the individual leaf signers rather than with a single aggregate public key representing the subgroup.

NestedMuSig2 provides recursive composition by allowing a participant public key at one aggregation node to be the child of a Musig2 aggregation node. Repeating this construction forms a tree of signing groups whose root is represented by a single aggregate public key. 

The construction preserves the external BIP340 interface. The completed protocol produces a BIP340 Schnorr signature under the root aggregate public key, and ordinary BIP340 verification does not require knowledge of the underlying signer tree. In particular, a participant represented by an aggregate public key need not reveal to participants outside that subgroup whether that public key represents an individual signer or a further nested MuSig2 group.

NestedMuSig2 remains an ''n''-of-''n'' construction at each MuSig2 aggregation node. Nesting does not provide ''t''-of-''n'' threshold signing; each MuSig2 node on the signing tree must ultimately include every participant required for the signing session.

Nested signing retains MuSig2's nonce-contribution and partial-signature stages, while contributions are recursively processed through the aggregation tree. This specification defines the additional key, nonce, session, signing, partial-signature verification, and signature-aggregation rules required to perform that recursive composition while producing a BIP340-compatible final signature.

==Specification==

This specification builds directly on [https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0327.mediawiki BIP327]. Unless explicitly stated otherwise, the notation, secp256k1 constants, point operations, serialization functions, and tagged-hash construction defined in BIP327 apply to this specification. In particular, this specification uses the BIP327 functions ''int(x)'', ''bytes(k, x)'', ''xbytes'', ''cbytes'', ''cbytes_ext'', ''cpoint'', ''cpoint_ext'', and ''has_even_y'', and the tagged hash construction ''hash<sub>tag</sub>(x)''.

The following BIP327 algorithms are used unchanged:
* ''IndividualPubkey''
* ''KeySort''
* ''KeyAgg''
* ''KeyAggCoeff''
* ''GetXonlyPubkey''
* ''GetPlainPubkey''
* ''ApplyTweak''
* ''NonceGen''
* ''NonceAgg''

All input requirements, failure conditions, serialization rules, and blame requirements for those algorithms apply whenever this specification invokes them.

The [https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0327.mediawiki#session-context BIP327 Session Context] and the algorithms ''GetSessionValues'', ''GetSessionKeyAggCoeff'', ''Sign'', ''PartialSigVerify'', ''PartialSigVerifyInternal'', and ''PartialSigAgg'' are replaced by the nested versions specified below. This specification additionally defines ''NonceAggExt'' for converting the internal aggregate nonce of a nested group into the first-round nonce contribution by which that group is represented at its parent aggregation node. This specification reuses only the BIP327 algorithms explicitly identified above. This specification does not specify other BIP327 signing algorithms, including DeterministicSign, for NestedMuSig2 sessions.

As in BIP327, an algorithm instruction to ''fail'' means the algorithm terminates without producing its normal output. An instruction to ''fail and blame'' a party additionally identifies the party whose invalid protocol contribution caused the failure. This specification does not require a particular API error type or serialization for such failures.

The [https://eprint.iacr.org/2026/223 Nested MuSig2] paper describes its construction over an abstract prime-order group. This specification instantiates that construction over secp256k1 using BIP327 key aggregation, BIP327's two-nonce representation, and the concrete tagged hashes specified below. This specification defines Bitcoin-specific serialization and aggregate-key tweaking rules that are not part of the abstract construction in the paper.

===Notation===

The following notation is used in addition to the notation of BIP327. A signing session is described from the perspective of one leaf signer and the unique path from that leaf to the root aggregation node.

The symbol ''p'' denotes the order of the prime-order group in the Nested MuSig2 paper. In this specification, the corresponding scalar modulus is the secp256k1 group order ''n''. This is distinct from the BIP327 constant ''p'', which denotes the secp256k1 field size.

The paper uses an abstract key-aggregation hash ''H<sub>agg</sub>'', a message-independent intermediate nonce hash ''H<sub>non</sub>'', a distinct message-dependent root nonce hash ''H̅<sub>non</sub>'', and a signature challenge hash ''H<sub>sig</sub>''. 

This specification instantiates their roles as follows:
* Key aggregation uses the optimized BIP327 ''KeyAgg'' and ''KeyAggCoeff'' construction independently at every aggregation node.
* The message-independent intermediate nonce hash is instantiated by ''hash<sub>NestedMuSig/aggnoncecoef</sub>''.
* The message-dependent root nonce hash is instantiated by the unchanged BIP327 ''hash<sub>MuSig/noncecoef</sub>'' computation.
* The signature challenge is instantiated by ''hash<sub>BIP0340/challenge</sub>''.
* ''&Lambda;'' is the number of aggregation nodes on the path from the leaf signer to the root, with ''&Lambda; &ge; 1''. Levels are indexed ''d = 0, ..., &Lambda;−1'' from the root toward the leaf. Level ''0'' is the root aggregation node and level ''&Lambda;−1'' is the aggregation node in which the leaf signer participates directly. Thus, ''&Lambda; = 1'' represents the flat BIP327 case. Different leaves in the same signer tree can have different values of ''&Lambda;''.
* The following values are defined relative to the leaf signer whose computation is being described. They are not global values associated with all nodes at a particular tree depth.
** ''pk<sub>d</sub>'' is the 33-byte plain public key by which the signer is represented at level ''d''. At level ''&Lambda;−1'', ''pk<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub>'' is the signer's individual plain public key. For ''d < &Lambda;−1'', ''pk<sub>d</sub>'' is the plain aggregate public key of the aggregation node on the signer's path. It corresponds to ''pk<sub>1,d</sub>'' in the Nested MuSig2 paper.
** ''T<sub>d</sub>'' is the multiset of all other participant plain public keys at level ''d'', excluding the distinguished participant occurrence represented by ''pk<sub>d</sub>''. An element of ''T<sub>d</sub>'' may represent either an individual signer or a nested signing group.<br>Duplicate public keys are permitted as in BIP327. Therefore ''T<sub>d</sub>'' may contain one or more occurrences whose 33-byte serialization is equal to ''pk<sub>d</sub>''. ''T<sub>d</sub>'' may also be empty.
** ''L<sub>d</sub>'' is the lexicographically sorted BIP327 key list formed from exactly one distinguished occurrence of ''pk<sub>d</sub>'' together with every occurrence in ''T<sub>d</sub>''.<br>For ''d > 0'', let ''keyagg_ctx<sub>d</sub> = KeyAgg(L<sub>d</sub>)'' and ''pk<sub>d−1</sub> = GetPlainPubkey(keyagg_ctx<sub>d</sub>)''.<br>Thus, ''pk<sub>d−1</sub>'' is the 33-byte plain aggregate public key by which the level-''d'' aggregation node participates at level ''d−1''.<br>''GetPlainPubkey(KeyAgg(L<sub>0</sub>))'' is the root aggregate plain public key.
** ''a<sub>d</sub>'' is the BIP327 key-aggregation coefficient ''a<sub>d</sub> = KeyAggCoeff(L<sub>d</sub>, pk<sub>d</sub>)''.<br>The product ''a<sub>0</sub>·a<sub>1</sub>·...·a<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub> mod n'' is the leaf signer's recursive key-aggregation coefficient.
* ''out<sub>d</sub>'' is the 66-byte internal aggregate nonce of the aggregation node at level ''d'' on the signer's path. It is the output of BIP327 ''NonceAgg'' applied to the first-round contributions of that node's participants.<br>For ''d > 0'', ''out<sub>d</sub>'' is not itself the contribution sent to the parent node. Instead, the node is represented at level ''d−1'' by ''NonceAggExt(out<sub>d</sub>, pk<sub>d−1</sub>)''.<br>The sequence ''(out<sub>0</sub>, ..., out<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub>)'' is called the signer's '''nonce path'''.
* For ''d = 1, ..., &Lambda;−1'', ''b<sub>d</sub>'' is the message-independent intermediate nonce-binding factor derived from ''out<sub>d</sub>'' and the complete 33-byte plain aggregate public key ''pk<sub>d−1</sub>''. It is the same coefficient used by ''NonceAggExt'' when constructing the internal node's external nonce.
* ''b<sub>0</sub>'' is the root nonce-binding factor computed according to BIP327 from ''out<sub>0</sub>'', the final root X-only aggregate public key, and the message. If root-level aggregate-key tweaks are applied, use the public key after those tweaks.<br>''b<sub>0</sub>'' is the only nonce-binding factor that commits directly to the message.
* ''b&#780;'' is the accumulated nonce-binding factor ''b&#780; = b<sub>0</sub>·b<sub>1</sub>·...·b<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub> mod n''.<br>Because this specification uses the BIP327 two-nonce construction, ''b&#780;'' is the coefficient multiplying the leaf signer's second secret nonce in its nested partial-signature equation.
* ''c'' is the BIP340 challenge ''c = int(hash<sub>BIP0340/challenge</sub>(xbytes(R) || xbytes(Q) || m)) mod n'', where ''Q'' is the final root aggregate public key and ''R'' is the final effective nonce point.
* ''c&#780;'' is the accumulated challenge coefficient ''c&#780; = c·a<sub>0</sub>·a<sub>1</sub>·...·a<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub> mod n''. It is the coefficient multiplying the leaf signer's secret-key contribution.
* Let ''out<sub>0</sub> = cbytes_ext(R<sub>1,0</sub>) || cbytes_ext(R<sub>2,0</sub>)''. Compute ''R' = R<sub>1,0</sub> + b<sub>0</sub>·R<sub>2,0</sub>''.<br>If ''R'' is the point at infinity, let ''R = G''; otherwise, let ''R = R''. This is the unchanged BIP327 root effective-nonce rule.<br>Intermediate binding factors do not appear explicitly in this root expression because they have already been incorporated into nested nonce contributions by preceding invocations of ''NonceAggExt''.


===Tagged Hashes===

Tagged hashes use the BIP340 construction ''SHA256(SHA256(tag) || SHA256(tag) || x)'', where ''tag'' is encoded as a UTF-8 byte string.

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Tag string !! Purpose
|-
| <code>KeyAgg list</code>, <code>KeyAgg coefficient</code>
| BIP327 key aggregation, performed independently at every aggregation node.
|-
| <code>MuSig/aux</code>
| Auxiliary-randomness processing in the unchanged BIP327 ''NonceGen''.
|-
| <code>MuSig/nonce</code>
| Secret-nonce derivation in the unchanged BIP327 ''NonceGen''.
|-
| <code>NestedMuSig/aggnoncecoef</code>
| Message-independent intermediate nonce-binding factors ''b''<sub>1</sub>, ..., ''b''<sub>Λ−1</sub>, and ''NonceAggExt''.
|-
| <code>MuSig/noncecoef</code>
| Message-dependent root nonce-binding factor ''b''<sub>0</sub>, computed exactly as in BIP327.
|-
| <code>BIP0340/challenge</code>
| Final Schnorr challenge, computed as specified in BIP340 and BIP327.
|}

The intermediate tag <code>NestedMuSig/aggnoncecoef</code> and the root tag <code>MuSig/noncecoef</code> instantiate distinct random-oracle roles and MUST remain domain-separated. In particular, the intermediate computation does not include the message, whereas the root computation does.

Using the unchanged <code>MuSig/noncecoef</code> computation at the root ensures that, when ''&Lambda; = 1'', no intermediate nonce-binding factor is computed and the root nonce processing is the BIP327 computation. For the same sorted root public-key list, tweak sequence, aggregate nonce, and message, the resulting flat session therefore uses the same key aggregation, nonce coefficient, effective nonce, and challenge as BIP327.

The key-aggregation tags are unchanged from BIP327. Therefore, each aggregation node produces the same aggregate public key that BIP327 produces for the same ordered list of 33-byte plain public keys.

The final challenge is computed exactly using the BIP340 challenge hash and encoding. Together with the nested signing and partial-signature aggregation rules specified below, this causes the final 64-byte signature to satisfy the ordinary BIP340 verification equation under the root X-only aggregate public key.

===Key Generation and Aggregation===

This specification uses the BIP327 algorithms ''IndividualPubkey'', ''KeySort'', ''KeyAgg'', ''KeyAggCoeff'', ''GetPlainPubkey'', ''GetXonlyPubkey'', and ''ApplyTweak'' as specified in BIP327. Their input requirements, failure conditions, and serialization rules apply whenever they are invoked below.

The Nested MuSig2 paper defines recursive key aggregation over group elements. This specification instantiates that construction using BIP327 plain public keys and BIP327's optimized key-aggregation algorithm. As an interoperability convention, participant plain public keys are sorted with ''KeySort'' independently at each aggregation node before invoking ''KeyAgg''.

====Nested Key Aggregation====

Key aggregation is performed independently at every aggregation node. For a node at level ''d'' on a particular signer's path, let ''L<sub>d</sub>'' be the participant plain-public-key list for that node after sorting with ''KeySort''. The node's KeyAgg Context is ''keyagg_ctx<sub>d</sub> = KeyAgg(L<sub>d</sub>)''. Each aggregation node MUST compute a separate KeyAgg Context from exactly the participant occurrences belonging to that node. Duplicate participant public keys are permitted as specified by BIP327; sorting MUST preserve every occurrence. For every non-root aggregation node at level ''d > 0'', let ''pk<sub>d−1</sub> = GetPlainPubkey(keyagg_ctx<sub>d</sub>)''. The resulting 33-byte plain public key is the participant public key by which the level-''d'' node is represented in ''L<sub>d−1</sub>'' at its parent aggregation node.

The parent node's ''KeyAgg'' invocation consumes this plain public key in the same way it consumes any other participant plain public key. An internal node's KeyAgg Context itself is not an input to the parent's ''KeyAgg'' computation. In particular, the internal node's ''gacc'' and ''tacc'' values are not inherited by the parent KeyAgg Context. The parent independently derives its own ''gacc'' and ''tacc'' as part of its own BIP327 key-aggregation and tweaking operations.

Implementations MAY cache intermediate KeyAgg Contexts or other public metadata. Such cached state has no cryptographic role in the parent ''KeyAgg'' invocation beyond the internal aggregate plain public key derived from it.

====Intermediate Aggregate Public Keys====

An intermediate aggregate public key MUST be represented by the 33-byte BIP327 plain-public-key encoding returned by ''GetPlainPubkey''. It MUST NOT be converted to an X-only public key before being used as a participant key in a parent ''KeyAgg'' invocation. For an intermediate aggregate point ''Q'', ''GetPlainPubkey'' returns ''cbytes(Q)'', which preserves the parity of ''Q''. The corresponding X-only encoding does not preserve that information and therefore does not uniquely identify the same group element. The recursive key aggregation defined here requires the actual internal aggregate group element as the participant public key at the next aggregation level.

Intermediate aggregate public keys are independent of a particular signing session and MAY be computed before signing. A participant that knows the corresponding public-key subtree can derive an intermediate aggregate public key locally. A participant that does not know that subtree MAY instead receive the 33-byte aggregate plain public key as the participant key representing the nested subgroup. The recursive signing algorithms do not require disclosure of the subgroup's internal participant keys to parties outside that subgroup.

====Root Aggregation====

The root aggregation node uses the same key-aggregation procedure as every other node. Let ''L<sub>0</sub>'' be the sorted list of root-level participant plain public keys. The untweaked root KeyAgg Context is ''keyagg_ctx<sub>0</sub> = KeyAgg(L<sub>0</sub>)''. Without aggregate-key tweaks, the root aggregate public key used for BIP340 verification is ''aggpk = GetXonlyPubkey(keyagg_ctx<sub>0</sub>)''.

====Aggregate-Key Tweaking====

The Nested MuSig2 construction referenced by this specification does not define aggregate-key tweaking. This specification also supports the BIP327 aggregate-key tweaking mechanism only at the root aggregation node. If the application specifies root-level aggregate-key tweaks, it MUST apply them sequentially to ''keyagg_ctx<sub>0</sub>'' using BIP327 ''ApplyTweak''. Any participants who act as an aggregator at the root level MUST use the same ordered tweak sequence and the same ''is_xonly_t'' value for each tweak. For tweaks ''tweak<sub>1</sub>, ..., tweak<sub>v</sub>'', let ''keyagg_ctx<sub>0,0</sub> = keyagg_ctx<sub>0</sub>'' and, for ''i = 1, ..., v'', ''keyagg_ctx<sub>0,i</sub> = ApplyTweak(keyagg_ctx<sub>0,i−1</sub>, tweak<sub>i</sub>, is_xonly_t<sub>i</sub>)''. Fail if any invocation of ''ApplyTweak'' fails according to BIP327.

After all tweaks are applied, let ''keyagg_ctx<sub>root</sub> = keyagg_ctx<sub>0,v</sub>'' when ''v > 0'', and let ''keyagg_ctx<sub>root</sub> = keyagg_ctx<sub>0</sub>'' when ''v = 0''. The final root X-only aggregate public key is ''aggpk = GetXonlyPubkey(keyagg_ctx<sub>root</sub>)''. This 32-byte X-only public key is the public key under which the final BIP340 signature is verified. The same final root KeyAgg Context, including its ''gacc'' and ''tacc'' values, MUST be used by the signing, partial-signature verification, and final root partial-signature aggregation algorithms defined below.

''ApplyTweak'' MUST NOT be applied to the KeyAgg Context of a non-root aggregation node. The nested signing and intermediate partial-signature aggregation algorithms in this specification account for recursive key-aggregation coefficients, but do not define the additional parity and tweak terms required if an intermediate aggregate key were modified with ''ApplyTweak''. Intermediate aggregate-key tweaking is therefore outside the scope of this specification. This restriction applies only to BIP327 aggregate-key tweaking at a non-root aggregation node. It does not restrict how a leaf signer derives or otherwise constructs its individual secret key and corresponding plain public key before supplying that public key to the NestedMuSig2 protocol.

===Nonce Generation===

Each leaf signer generates its secret nonce and public nonce using the BIP327 algorithm ''NonceGen'' unchanged. All input requirements, optional-argument encodings, failure conditions, tagged hashes, and output semantics of BIP327 ''NonceGen'' apply. In particular, nonce generation uses the BIP327 tagged hashes <code>MuSig/aux</code> and <code>MuSig/nonce</code>. NestedMuSig2 does not introduce a separate tagged hash for leaf nonce generation. Nested-specific domain separation is introduced later, when ''NonceAggExt'' processes aggregate nonces. Nonce generation itself does not depend on the leaf signer's nesting depth. A leaf signer runs the same ''NonceGen'' algorithm whether it participates directly at the root or through one or more nested aggregation nodes.

For a leaf signer whose path contains ''Λ'' aggregation levels, the arguments supplied to ''NonceGen'' have the following semantics:
* The mandatory ''pk'' argument MUST be the signer's 33-byte individual plain public key ''pk<sub>Λ−1</sub>''. It MUST NOT be replaced by an intermediate subgroup aggregate public key or by the root aggregate public key.
* The optional ''sk'' argument, when provided, MUST be the secret signing key corresponding to ''pk<sub>Λ−1</sub>''. It SHOULD be supplied whenever the secret key is available to the nonce-generation component.
* The optional ''aggpk'' argument, when provided, MUST be the 32-byte X-only root aggregate public key after all root-level key aggregation and aggregate-key tweaks defined for the signing session have been applied. Equivalently, ''aggpk = GetXonlyPubkey(keyagg_ctx<sub>root</sub>)''. An intermediate subgroup aggregate public key MUST NOT be supplied as ''aggpk''. If the final root aggregate public key has not yet been determined when nonce generation is performed, ''aggpk'' MAY be omitted as permitted by BIP327.
* The optional message ''m'' SHOULD be supplied if the message is already determined when ''NonceGen'' is invoked. It MAY be omitted when nonce generation is performed before the message is known. As in BIP327, an omitted message is distinct from a present message whose length is zero.
* The optional ''extra_in'' argument MAY contain application-specific contextual data as described by BIP327, such as a session identifier, non-repeating counter, or other session-specific state. Applications MAY include NestedMuSig2-specific session context in this value as a defense-in-depth measure, but this specification does not define a mandatory encoding for such context.

For the algorithms and test vectors in this specification, the secret nonce is represented as the 97-byte array ''secnonce = bytes(32, k<sub>1</sub>) ||bytes(32, k<sub>2</sub>) || pk<sub>Λ−1</sub>'', and the public nonce is represented as the 66-byte array ''pubnonce = cbytes(k<sub>1</sub>⋅G) || cbytes(k<sub>2</sub>⋅G)''. The ''secnonce'' is secret local signer state and MUST NOT be transmitted to another participant. Implementations MAY represent it internally using an opaque handle or another data structure instead of the 97-byte representation, provided that the two nonce scalars and the individual public key are retained with the semantics required by ''Sign''. The ''pubnonce'' is public protocol data. It is the leaf signer's first-round nonce contribution to the aggregation node in which the leaf directly participates.

As required by BIP327, the internal value <code>rand'</code> used by ''NonceGen'' MUST be a freshly drawn, unbiased, uniformly random 32-byte value obtained from a high-quality cryptographically secure random generator. Nonce scalars MUST NOT be generated deterministically solely from the message, public keys, signing tree, or other signing-session parameters controlled or influenced by an adversary. The optional arguments to ''NonceGen'' provide defense in depth against certain failures of the randomness source, but they do not remove the requirement for fresh high-quality randomness.

A ''secnonce'' MUST be used as input to at most one invocation of ''Sign''. It MUST be considered consumed even if that invocation subsequently fails. The same secret nonce MUST NOT be reused in another NestedMuSig2 session, a BIP327 MuSig2 session, or any other signing protocol. Implementations SHOULD enforce single use by keeping secret nonces behind opaque consuming handles or equivalent state, marking the nonce as consumed before performing signing operations, and securely erasing secret nonce scalars after they are no longer required. Only leaf signers invoke ''NonceGen''. An internal aggregation node representing a nested signing group derives its first-round contribution from its participants' public nonce contributions using ''NonceAgg'' followed, when applicable, by ''NonceAggExt''. Such a node MUST NOT generate an independent replacement nonce with ''NonceGen''.

This specification does not define NestedMuSig2 variants of BIP327 ''CounterNonceGen'' or ''DeterministicSign''. Those algorithms MUST NOT be assumed to be applicable to NestedMuSig2 sessions solely because this specification reuses BIP327 ''NonceGen''. Support for such nonce-generation variants requires separate specification and security analysis.

===Nonce Aggregation===

The BIP327 algorithm ''NonceAgg'' is used unchanged at every aggregation node. Its input requirements, failure conditions, serialization rules, and contributor-blame rules apply whenever it is invoked.

During the first signing stage, nonce aggregation proceeds recursively from the leaves toward the root. A participant at an aggregation node contributes one of the following:
* A direct leaf signer contributes the 66-byte ''pubnonce'' returned by ''NonceGen''.
* A nested internal aggregation node contributes the 66-byte external nonce returned by ''NonceAggExt''.

For an aggregation node at level ''d'', let ''L<sub>d</sub> = (pk<sub>1,d</sub>, ..., pk<sub>u,d</sub>)'' be its sorted participant public-key list. Let ''contribution<sub>1..u</sub>'' contain exactly one nonce contribution for each corresponding participant occurrence in ''L<sub>d</sub>''. Implementations MUST retain an unambiguous association between each public-key occurrence and its nonce contribution. This is required even when duplicate public keys occur. The ordering does not affect the group sum computed by ''NonceAgg'', but the association is required for contribution attribution and later partial-signature verification. The node computes ''out<sub>d</sub> = NonceAgg(contribution<sub>1</sub>, ..., contribution<sub>u</sub>)''. The 66-byte value ''out<sub>d</sub>'' is called the node's '''internal aggregate nonce'''. Its two components are aggregate points and therefore use the BIP327 ''cbytes_ext'' representation. For a non-root node, where ''0 < d < &lambda; - 1'', let ''pk<sub>d−1</sub> = GetPlainPubkey(KeyAgg(L<sub>d</sub>))''. The node computes ''extnonce<sub>d</sub> = NonceAggExt(out<sub>d</sub>, pk<sub>d−1</sub>)'' and supplies ''extnonce<sub>d</sub>'' as its nonce contribution to its parent aggregation node at level ''d−1''.

At the root, ''out<sub>0</sub>'' is retained as the root internal aggregate nonce. No external nonce is required because the root has no parent, and this specification therefore does not invoke ''NonceAggExt'' on ''out<sub>0</sub>''. The root nonce-binding factor is computed according to BIP327: ''b<sub>0</sub> = int(hash<sub>MuSig/noncecoef</sub>(out<sub>0</sub> || xbytes(Q) || m)) mod n'', where ''Q'' is the root aggregate public key after all root-level tweaks have been applied.

For the same sorted root public-key list, tweak sequence, aggregate nonce, and message, root nonce aggregation and root nonce processing therefore coincide with BIP327.

====Internal Aggregate Nonces and the Nonce Path====

Every aggregation node MUST preserve the exact internal aggregate nonce ''out<sub>d</sub>'' used in the signing session until that session completes or aborts. An implementation MAY retain ''out<sub>d</sub>'' directly or reconstruct it from authenticated first-round session state, provided that the reconstructed value is exactly the value from which the node's external nonce was derived. Before producing a partial signature, a leaf signer MUST obtain or reconstruct the sequence ''nonce_path = (out<sub>0</sub>, ..., out<sub>Λ−1</sub>)'' for the aggregation nodes on its path from the root to the leaf.

Every element of ''nonce_path'' MUST be an internal aggregate nonce produced by ''NonceAgg''. An external nonce returned by ''NonceAggExt'' MUST NOT be substituted for an internal aggregate nonce in this path. For every non-root node, the ''out<sub>d</sub>'' used in the leaf's nonce path MUST be the exact value from which that node derived the external nonce supplied to its parent.

This specification does not prescribe a transport mechanism for distributing the nonce path. Aggregators MAY forward path prefixes toward leaves, or participants MAY reconstruct the required values from authenticated signing transcripts.

====External Nonce Aggregation====

Algorithm ''NonceAggExt(aggnonce, pk_agg)'':
* Inputs:
** ''aggnonce'': the 66-byte internal aggregate nonce produced by ''NonceAgg'' for a non-root aggregation node.
** ''pk_agg'': the 33-byte BIP327 plain aggregate public key by which that node is represented at its parent.
* ''Fail'' if ''len(aggnonce) ≠ 66''.
* ''Fail'' if ''len(pk_agg) ≠ 33''.
* Let ''R'<sub>1</sub> = cpoint_ext(aggnonce[0:33])''; ''Fail'' if that fails.
* Let ''R'<sub>2</sub> = cpoint_ext(aggnonce[33:66])''; ''Fail'' if that fails.
* Let ''b = int(hash<sub>NestedMuSig/aggnoncecoef</sub>(aggnonce || xbytes(pk_agg))) mod n''.
* Let ''R<sub>1</sub> = R'<sub>1</sub>''.
* Let ''R<sub>2</sub> = b⋅R'<sub>2</sub>''.
* ''Fail'' if ''R<sub>1</sub>'' or ''R<sub>2</sub>'' is the point at infinity.
* Return ''cbytes(R<sub>1</sub>) || cbytes(R<sub>2</sub>)''.

For the BIP327 two-nonce instantiation, only the second internal aggregate nonce point is multiplied by ''b''. This is the specialization of the NestedMuSig2 rule ''R<sub>j</sub> = b<sup>j−1</sup>⋅R'<sub>j</sub>''. Therefore, ''R<sub>1</sub> = R'<sub>1</sub>'' and ''R<sub>2</sub> = b⋅R'<sub>2</sub>''. As external nonces propagate toward the root, repeated invocations of ''NonceAggExt'' multiply the contribution of a leaf's second nonce point by the intermediate binding factors on that leaf's path. The root binding factor is applied during root nonce processing, giving the accumulated coefficient ''b̌ = b<sub>0</sub>·b<sub>1</sub>·...·b<sub>Λ−1</sub> mod n''.

====Points at Infinity====

An internal aggregate nonce produced by BIP327 ''NonceAgg'' may contain the point at infinity, represented by 33 zero bytes using ''cbytes_ext''. Accordingly, ''NonceAggExt'' parses the two components of its input using ''cpoint_ext''. An external nonce, however, is used as an ordinary participant nonce in the parent's unchanged BIP327 ''NonceAgg'' invocation. Its two components must therefore be ordinary finite compressed points. Consequently, ''NonceAggExt'' fails if either of its output components would be the point at infinity. It MUST NOT replace an infinite component with ''G'' or any other point. The scalar ''b'' MUST NOT be replaced with a nonzero value when the tagged hash yields ''b = 0''. If ''b = 0'' causes an external nonce component to be the point at infinity, ''NonceAggExt'' fails. For honestly generated session values, such events occur only with negligible probability. This non-root behavior is distinct from BIP327 root nonce processing. At the root, ''out<sub>0</sub>'' remains an aggregate nonce and its components are parsed using ''cpoint_ext''. After computing ''R' = R<sub>1,0</sub> + b<sub>0</sub>⋅R<sub>2,0</sub>'', the unchanged BIP327 rule applies: if ''R''' is the point at infinity, the final effective nonce is set to ''R = G''.

===Session Context===

The '''Session Context''' of a leaf signer contains the public information required to reconstruct the NestedMuSig2 signing values along that signer's path to the root. It consists of:
* ''nonce_path'': the sequence ''(out<sub>0</sub>, ..., out<sub>Λ−1</sub>)'' of internal aggregate nonces at the aggregation nodes on the signer's path, ordered from the root toward the leaf. Each ''out<sub>d</sub>'' is a 66-byte BIP327 aggregate nonce of the form ''cbytes_ext(R<sub>1,d</sub>) || cbytes_ext(R<sub>2,d</sub>)''. Either component may encode the point at infinity as 33 zero bytes, as permitted for BIP327 aggregate nonces.
* ''cosigner_key_path'': the sequence ''(T<sub>0</sub>, ..., T<sub>Λ−1</sub>)'' of cosigner plain-public-key multisets at the aggregation nodes on the signer's path, ordered from the root toward the leaf.<br>Each ''T<sub>d</sub>'' contains one 33-byte BIP327 plain public key for every participant occurrence at level ''d'' other than the distinguished occurrence represented by ''pk<sub>d</sub>''. <br>An element of ''T<sub>d</sub>'' may represent either an individual signer or a nested subgroup. The algorithms defined by this specification do not require distinguishing those cases. <br>''T<sub>d</sub>'' MAY be empty. It MAY contain one or more public-key occurrences whose 33-byte serialization equals ''pk<sub>d</sub>'', because BIP327 permits duplicate participant public keys.<br>The ordering used to represent ''T<sub>d</sub>'' has no cryptographic significance. The corresponding participant list is constructed as ''L<sub>d</sub> = KeySort({pk<sub>d</sub>} ⊎ T<sub>d</sub>)'', where ⊎ denotes multiset union and inserts exactly one distinguished occurrence of ''pk<sub>d</sub>''.
* ''tweak<sub>1..v</sub>'': the ordered sequence of ''v'' 32-byte BIP327 aggregate-key tweaks applied at the root aggregation node, with ''0 ≤ v < 2<sup>32</sup>''.
* ''is_xonly_t<sub>1..v</sub>'': ''v'' booleans, one BIP327 tweak-mode flag corresponding to each element of ''tweak<sub>1..v</sub>''.
* ''m'': the message to be signed, represented as a byte array.

All fields of the Session Context are public. The Session Context contains no secret key or secret nonce material. The sequences ''nonce_path'' and ''cosigner_key_path'' MUST have the same length ''Λ'', with ''Λ ≥ 1''. For every level ''d'', the resulting list ''L<sub>d</sub>'' MUST satisfy the BIP327 ''KeySort'' and ''KeyAgg'' size requirement ''0 < len(L<sub>d</sub>) < 2<sup>32</sup>''. The signer reconstructs ''pk<sub>d</sub>'' recursively from its individual plain public key and the lower-level entries of ''cosigner_key_path''. Consequently, Session Contexts are path-local: different leaves in the same NestedMuSig2 tree generally have different ''nonce_path'' and ''cosigner_key_path'' values. A leaf does not need the public-key structure of subtrees that are not on its own aggregation path; such a subtree may be represented solely by its aggregate plain public key in the appropriate ''T<sub>d</sub>''.

If an implementation associates participant identities or blame information with public-key occurrences, that association MUST distinguish occurrences, not just distinct public-key byte strings. Applying ''KeySort'' MUST NOT lose this occurrence-level association. Implementations MAY cache values derived from a Session Context, including values produced by ''GetSessionValues''. A cached value MUST only be reused with the exact Session Context from which it was derived. Implementations SHOULD treat an accepted Session Context as immutable. Although confidentiality of the Session Context is not required, the Session Context and any cached values derived from it MUST be protected against unauthorized modification before and during signing. Before releasing a partial signature, a signer MUST ensure that the message, root aggregate-key tweak policy, and cosigner-key path correspond to the authorization it intends to make. The signer MUST use the exact ''nonce_path'' associated with the first-round state for that signing session.

This specification does not require a leaf signer to possess every individual public nonce or the complete public-key tree in order to independently reconstruct every internal aggregate nonce. An application MAY provide such transcript information for stronger local validation, but NestedMuSig2 security does not depend on a particular transcript-transport or coordinator architecture.

===Signing===

The internal algorithm ''GetSessionValues'' derives the public values required to produce and verify a leaf signer's partial signature. It reconstructs the key-aggregation nodes on the signer's path from the leaf toward the root, derives the corresponding key-aggregation and intermediate nonce-binding coefficients, applies any root-level aggregate-key tweaks, and computes the root BIP327 nonce coefficient and BIP340 challenge.

For a signer with ''Λ'' aggregation levels, the algorithm derives the accumulated nonce-binding coefficient ''b̌ = b<sub>0</sub>·b<sub>1</sub>·...·b<sub>Λ−1</sub> mod n'' and the accumulated challenge coefficient ''č = c·a<sub>0</sub>·a<sub>1</sub>·...·a<sub>Λ−1</sub> mod n''.

Internal Algorithm ''GetSessionValues(session_ctx, pk)'':
* Inputs:
  ** ''session_ctx'': a Session Context as defined above.
  ** ''pk'': the leaf signer's 33-byte BIP327 plain public key.
* Let ''(nonce_path, cosigner_key_path, tweak<sub>1..v</sub>, is_xonly_t<sub>1..v</sub>, m) = session_ctx''.
* Let ''Λ = len(cosigner_key_path)''.
* ''Fail'' if ''Λ < 1''.
* ''Fail'' if ''len(nonce_path) ≠ Λ''.
* ''Fail'' if ''len(tweak<sub>1..v</sub>) ≠ len(is_xonly_t<sub>1..v</sub>)''.
* ''Fail'' if ''len(pk) ≠ 33''.
* For ''d = 0, ..., Λ−1'':
** ''Fail'' if ''len(nonce_path[d]) ≠ 66''.
** Let ''R'<sub>1,d</sub> = cpoint_ext(nonce_path[d][0:33])'', ''R'<sub>2,d</sub> = cpoint_ext(nonce_path[d][33:66])''; fail if that fails and blame the level-''d'' nonce aggregator for invalid aggnonce.
* Let ''pk<sub>Λ−1</sub> = pk''.
* Let ''L<sub>Λ−1</sub> = KeySort({pk<sub>Λ−1</sub>} ⊎ T<sub>Λ−1</sub>)'', where ⊎ denotes multiset union and inserts exactly one distinguished occurrence of ''pk<sub>Λ−1</sub>''.
* Let ''a<sub>Λ−1</sub> = KeyAggCoeff(L<sub>Λ−1</sub>, pk<sub>Λ−1</sub>)''.
* Let ''keyagg_ctx = KeyAgg(L<sub>Λ−1</sub>)''; fail if ''KeyAgg'' fails according to BIP327.
* For ''d = Λ−2, ..., 0'':
** Let ''pk<sub>d</sub> = GetPlainPubkey(keyagg_ctx)''.
** Let ''b<sub>d+1</sub> = int(hash<sub>NestedMuSig/aggnoncecoef</sub>(nonce_path[d+1] || xbytes(pk<sub>d</sub>))) mod n''.
** ''Fail'' if ''R'<sub>1,d+1</sub>'' is the point at infinity.
** Let ''R<sub>2,ext</sub> = b<sub>d+1</sub>⋅R'<sub>2,d+1</sub>''.
** ''Fail'' if ''R<sub>2,ext</sub>'' is the point at infinity.
** Let ''L<sub>d</sub> = KeySort({pk<sub>d</sub>} ⊎ T<sub>d</sub>)''.
** Let ''a<sub>d</sub> = KeyAggCoeff(L<sub>d</sub>, pk<sub>d</sub>)''.
** Let ''keyagg_ctx = KeyAgg(L<sub>d</sub>)''; fail if ''KeyAgg'' fails according to BIP327.
* For ''i = 1, ..., v'':
** Let ''keyagg_ctx = ApplyTweak(keyagg_ctx, tweak<sub>i</sub>, is_xonly_t<sub>i</sub>)''; fail if ''ApplyTweak'' fails according to BIP327.
* Let ''(Q, gacc, tacc) = keyagg_ctx''.
* Let ''b<sub>0</sub> = int(hash<sub>MuSig/noncecoef</sub>(nonce_path[0] || xbytes(Q) || m)) mod n''.
* Let ''R'<sub>1</sub> = cpoint_ext(nonce_path[0][0:33])''; if that fails, fail.
* Let ''R'<sub>2</sub> = cpoint_ext(nonce_path[0][33:66])''; if that fails, fail.
* Let ''R' = R'<sub>1</sub> + b<sub>0</sub>⋅R'<sub>2</sub>''.
* If ''R''' is the point at infinity, let ''R = G''. Otherwise, let ''R = R'''.
* Let ''b̌ = b<sub>0</sub>·b<sub>1</sub>·...·b<sub>Λ−1</sub> mod n''.
* Let ''c = int(hash<sub>BIP0340/challenge</sub>(xbytes(R) || xbytes(Q) || m)) mod n''.
* Let ''č = c·a<sub>0</sub>·a<sub>1</sub>·...·a<sub>Λ−1</sub> mod n''.
* Return ''(Q, gacc, tacc, b̌, R, č)''.

For ''Λ = 1'', no intermediate nonce-binding coefficient is computed. The sole key-aggregation happens at level-''0'', whose output is the root aggregate public key at level''−1''. The root aggregate public key itself is not represented in ''cosigner_key_path''. For the same sorted level-''0'' public-key list, root tweak sequence, aggregate nonce, and message, the values ''Q'', ''gacc'', ''tacc'', ''b<sub>0</sub>'', ''R'', and ''c'' are the corresponding BIP327 session values. In this case, ''b̌ = b<sub>0</sub>'' and ''č = c·a<sub>0</sub>''.

We retain both ''c'' and ''č'' because they serve different roles. Leaf partial signing and leaf partial-signature verification use ''č'', which includes every key-aggregation coefficient on the leaf's path. Final root-level tweak aggregation uses the ordinary challenge ''c'', because BIP327's root tweak contribution is proportional to ''c·gacc·tacc'' and is not multiplied by the recursive leaf key-aggregation coefficients.

====Partial Signing====

The nested ''Sign'' algorithm follows the structure of BIP327 ''Sign'', but uses the accumulated nonce-binding and challenge coefficients returned by ''GetSessionValues''.

Algorithm ''Sign(secnonce, sk, session_ctx)'':
* Inputs:
** ''secnonce'': secret nonce state returned by ''NonceGen'' and not previously supplied to ''Sign''.
** ''sk'': the signer's 32-byte secret signing key.
** ''session_ctx'': the signer's Session Context.
* ''Fail'' if the supplied ''secnonce'' does not have the representation required by this specification or the implementation's equivalent opaque secret-nonce representation.
* Copy from ''secnonce'': ''k'<sub>1</sub>'', ''k'<sub>2</sub>'', and ''pk' ''. For the 97-byte reference representation, ''k'<sub>1</sub> = int(secnonce[0:32])'', ''k'<sub>2</sub> = int(secnonce[32:64])'', and ''pk' = secnonce[64:97]''.
* The secret nonce MUST now be marked consumed before performing any remaining operation that can fail. It MUST NOT be supplied to another invocation of ''Sign'', regardless of whether this invocation subsequently succeeds or fails. Implementations SHOULD securely erase the copied secret nonce scalars from persistent nonce state or use an API that consumes an opaque secret-nonce object.
* ''Fail'' if ''len(sk) ≠ 32''.
* ''Fail'' if ''k'<sub>i</sub> = 0'' or ''k'<sub>i</sub> ≥ n'' for ''i = 1, 2''.
* Let ''pk = IndividualPubkey(sk)''; fail if that fails.
* ''Fail'' if ''pk ≠ pk' ''.
* Let ''(Q, gacc, _, b̌, R, _, č) = GetSessionValues(session_ctx, pk)''; fail if that fails.
* If ''has_even_y(R)'', let ''k<sub>i</sub> = k'<sub>i</sub>'' for ''i = 1, 2''. Otherwise, let ''k<sub>i</sub> = n − k'<sub>i</sub>'' for ''i = 1, 2''.
* Let ''d' = int(sk)''. ''IndividualPubkey(sk)'' has already established that ''0 < d' < n''.
* Let ''g = 1'' if ''has_even_y(Q)'', and otherwise let ''g = −1 mod n''.
* Let ''d = g·gacc·d' mod n''.
* Let ''s = k<sub>1</sub> + b̌·k<sub>2</sub> + č·d mod n''.
* Let ''psig = bytes(32, s)''.
* Let ''pubnonce = cbytes(k'<sub>1</sub>⋅G) || cbytes(k'<sub>2</sub>⋅G)''.
* Run ''PartialSigVerifyInternal(psig, pubnonce, pk, session_ctx)''. If it fails, fail.
* Return the 32-byte partial signature ''psig''.

The second-round contribution of a leaf signer is only ''psig''. The effective root aggregate nonce ''R'' is public and is deterministically reconstructed from the Session Context by signers, partial-signature verifiers, and the root aggregator. The internal partial-signature verification step is part of the signing algorithm. It detects inconsistent session state or an incorrect local signing computation before releasing a partial signature.

===Partial Signature Verification===

''PartialSigVerify'' verifies the second-round contribution by which a participant is represented at a particular aggregation node. The participant may be either an individual leaf signer or a nested aggregation node.

For an individual leaf signer:
* ''pubnonce'' is the 66-byte public nonce returned by ''NonceGen'';
* ''pk'' is the leaf signer's 33-byte individual plain public key; and
* ''session_ctx'' is the leaf signer's complete Session Context.

For a nested aggregation node at level ''d > 0'':
* ''pubnonce'' is the node's 66-byte external nonce returned by ''NonceAggExt'';
* ''pk'' is the 33-byte plain aggregate public key ''pk<sub>d−1</sub>'' by which the node participates at level ''d−1''; and
* ''session_ctx'' is the Session Context truncated to the participant's position at level ''d−1''.

More precisely, the truncated Session Context contains ''nonce_path = (out<sub>0</sub>, ..., out<sub>d−1</sub>)'' and ''cosigner_key_path = (T<sub>0</sub>, ..., T<sub>d−1</sub>)'', together with the same root tweak sequence, tweak modes, and message as the complete signing session. In ''T<sub>d−1</sub>'', the participant occurrence represented by ''pk<sub>d−1</sub>'' is excluded as required by the Session Context definition.

Algorithm ''PartialSigVerify(psig, pubnonce, pk, session_ctx)'':
* Inputs:
** ''psig'': the participant's 32-byte partial signature.
** ''pubnonce'': the participant's 66-byte public nonce. For a nested aggregation node, this is its external nonce.
** ''pk'': the participant's 33-byte BIP327 plain public key.
** ''session_ctx'': the Session Context corresponding to the participant's position in the nested signer tree.
* Return failure if ''len(psig) ≠ 32''.
* Return failure if ''len(pubnonce) ≠ 66''.
* Return failure if ''len(pk) ≠ 33''.
* Let ''(Q, gacc, _, b̌, R, _, č) = GetSessionValues(session_ctx, pk)''; return failure if that fails.
* Let ''s = int(psig)''. Return failure if ''s ≥ n''.
* Let ''R<sub>*,1</sub> = cpoint(pubnonce[0:33])''; return failure if that fails.
* Let ''R<sub>*,2</sub> = cpoint(pubnonce[33:66])''; return failure if that fails.
* Let ''Ř' = R<sub>*,1</sub> + b̌⋅R<sub>*,2</sub>''.
* If ''has_even_y(R)'', let ''Ř = Ř' ''. Otherwise, let ''Ř = −Ř' ''.
* Let ''P = cpoint(pk)''. Return failure if that fails.
* Let ''g = 1'' if ''has_even_y(Q)'', and otherwise let ''g = −1 mod n''.
* Let ''g' = g·gacc mod n''.
* Return success if and only if ''s⋅G = Ř + (č·g' mod n)⋅P''.

For an individual leaf signer, this equation follows directly from the ''Sign'' algorithm: ''s = k<sub>1</sub> + b̌·k<sub>2</sub> + č·g·gacc·d' mod n''. For a nested aggregation node, the equation follows recursively. Assume that the required participant contributions at the node satisfy their respective verification equations. Adding those equations combines their nonce terms according to the node's ''NonceAgg'' result and combines their public-key terms according to the node's BIP327 ''KeyAgg'' equation. The node's ''NonceAggExt'' invocation applies the node's intermediate nonce-binding factor to the second aggregate nonce component. Therefore, the scalar sum of the participant partial signatures satisfies the same verification equation under the node's aggregate plain public key and external nonce when evaluated using the Session Context truncated at the node's parent.

This recursive property lets an aggregate signing node be treated by its parent like a single signing participant. As in BIP327, partial-signature verification exists primarily to identify disruptive participants. A partial signature is not a standalone signature and successful partial-signature verification MUST NOT be interpreted as proof of knowledge or possession of the secret key corresponding to ''pk''. If identifiable aborts are not required, an application MAY omit verification of received partial signatures before aggregation. Implementations SHOULD nevertheless perform the self-verification required by ''Sign'' before releasing locally generated partial signatures.

===Partial Signature Aggregation===

Second-round aggregation proceeds recursively from the leaves toward the root. At a non-root aggregation node, participant partial signatures are combined into one 32-byte partial signature representing that entire nested subgroup at its parent. At the root, the root-level participant contributions are aggregated using the unchanged BIP327 final partial-signature aggregation procedure.

====Intermediate Partial Signature Aggregation====

For a non-root aggregation node, let ''psig<sub>1..u</sub>'' contain exactly one second-round contribution for every participant occurrence at that node. Intermediate aggregate public keys are not tweaked. Consequently, intermediate aggregation consists only of scalar addition; no tweak contribution is added.

Algorithm ''PartialSigAggIntermediate(psig<sub>1..u</sub>)'':
* Inputs:
** The number ''u'' of participant contributions, with ''0 < u < 2<sup>32</sup>''.
** ''psig<sub>1..u</sub>'': one 32-byte partial signature for every participant occurrence at the aggregation node.
* For ''i = 1, ..., u'':
** If ''len(psig<sub>i</sub>) ≠ 32'', fail and blame participant occurrence ''i'' for an invalid partial signature.
** Let ''s<sub>i</sub> = int(psig<sub>i</sub>)''.
** If ''s<sub>i</sub> ≥ n'', fail and blame participant occurrence ''i'' for an invalid partial signature.
* Let ''s = s<sub>1</sub> + ... + s<sub>u</sub> mod n''.
* Return ''bytes(32, s)''.

The returned value is the partial signature that represents the aggregation node to its parent.

For a node at level ''d > 0'', this aggregate partial signature can be verified with ''PartialSigVerify'' using:
* the external nonce ''NonceAggExt(out<sub>d</sub>, pk<sub>d−1</sub>)'' as ''pubnonce'';
* the node's 33-byte aggregate plain public key ''pk<sub>d−1</sub>'' as ''pk''; and
* the Session Context truncated to levels ''0, ..., d−1''.

The node's external nonce already incorporates the intermediate nonce-binding factor ''b<sub>d</sub>''. Transformations introduced by nested descendants are already incorporated into the contributions aggregated in ''out<sub>d</sub>''. Consequently, the truncated Session Context does not include level ''d'' or any descendant level. An aggregator that wants identifiable aborts SHOULD run ''PartialSigVerify'' on every participant contribution before invoking ''PartialSigAggIntermediate''. ''PartialSigAggIntermediate'' itself validates only the partial-signature scalar encodings and does not establish that the supplied values satisfy their verification equations.

====Root Partial Signature Aggregation====

At the root, each root-level participant is represented by:
* one 33-byte BIP327 plain public key;
* one 66-byte BIP327-compatible participant public nonce; and
* one 32-byte partial signature.

For a direct leaf participant, these are its individual public key, ''NonceGen'' public nonce, and leaf partial signature. For a nested participant, these are its aggregate plain public key, external nonce, and intermediate aggregate partial signature. Let ''L<sub>0</sub>'' be the sorted root participant public-key list, and let ''out<sub>0</sub>'' be the root internal aggregate nonce previously computed from the corresponding root-level participant nonce contributions. Construct the ordinary BIP327 Session Context ''root_session_ctx = (out<sub>0</sub>, len(L<sub>0</sub>), L<sub>0</sub>, v, tweak<sub>1..v</sub>, is_xonly_t<sub>1..v</sub>, m)''. The root aggregator MUST supply exactly one 32-byte partial signature for every participant occurrence in ''L<sub>0</sub>''. Final signature aggregation is performed by invoking the BIP327 algorithm ''PartialSigAgg'' unchanged with the root-level partial signatures and ''root_session_ctx''.

In particular, BIP327 ''PartialSigAgg'':
* derives the final tweaked root KeyAgg Context;
* derives the root ''MuSig/noncecoef'' binding factor;
* derives the effective root nonce and applies the BIP327 point-at-infinity rule;
* computes the BIP340 challenge;
* sums the root-level partial-signature scalars;
* adds the root tweak contribution ''c·g·tacc mod n'' exactly once; and
* returns the 64-byte signature ''xbytes(R) || bytes(32, s)''.

No additional NestedMuSig2-specific scalar or tweak term is added during root aggregation. Provided that the root-level contributions are generated from one consistent signing session and all intermediate aggregations follow this specification, the output is an ordinary BIP340 signature under ''GetXonlyPubkey(keyagg_ctx<sub>root</sub>)'' for message ''m''. An implementation SHOULD verify the completed signature using ordinary BIP340 verification before releasing or relying on it.


==Rationale==

NestedMuSig2 is based on the recursive construction described in [[https://eprint.iacr.org/2026/223|Nested MuSig2]], but this specification must add concrete conventions that are not fixed by the abstract construction in the paper. In particular, this specification uses BIP327 public-key aggregation, secp256k1 point encodings, BIP340 tagged hashes, BIP327 nonce generation and aggregate-key tweaking, and explicit failure behavior.

The following subsections explain the principal design choices.

===Reuse of BIP327 Algorithms===

Where the nested construction does not require different behavior, this specification reuses BIP327 algorithms unchanged.

In particular, the specification reuses BIP327:
* plain-public-key encoding and parsing;
* key sorting and optimized key aggregation;
* leaf nonce generation;
* coordinate-wise nonce aggregation;
* aggregate-key tweaking at the root; and
* final root partial-signature aggregation.

The intent is to introduce only the operations required for recursive composition. A nested subgroup is reduced to a plain public key, public nonce, and partial signature before it is processed by its parent. At the root, these values therefore have the same external forms as the corresponding values of ordinary BIP327 participants. For a signing tree of depth ''Λ = 1'', no intermediate recursive operation is required. For the same sorted participant-key list, tweak sequence, aggregate nonce, and message, the root key aggregation, root nonce coefficient, effective nonce, challenge, and final partial-signature aggregation therefore use the BIP327 computations.

===Sorting at Every Aggregation Node===

BIP327 ''KeyAgg'' is order-dependent and provides ''KeySort'' for applications that require order-independent aggregation. This specification invokes ''KeySort'' independently at every aggregation node. This provides one canonical BIP327 participant-key ordering for each multiset of participant occurrences and avoids requiring every application to define an additional ordering convention for nested groups. Sorting is local to an aggregation node. An internal node first aggregates using its own sorted participant list, and the resulting aggregate plain public key then appears as one participant key in its parent's sorted list. Duplicate public-key occurrences remain distinct occurrences during this process.

===Separate Intermediate and Root Nonce Binding===

The Nested MuSig2 construction distinguishes intermediate nonce binding from root nonce binding. Intermediate aggregation uses a message-independent binding factor, while the root binding factor additionally commits to the message.

This specification instantiates these roles with separate tagged hashes:
* <code>NestedMuSig/aggnoncecoef</code> for intermediate binding; and
* <code>MuSig/noncecoef</code> for root binding.

The tags MUST remain distinct. Using a separate intermediate tag separates the two random-oracle roles. Retaining the existing <code>MuSig/noncecoef</code> calculation at the root preserves the BIP327 root computation in the flat ''Λ = 1'' case. Using <code>MuSig/noncecoef</code> at every aggregation level was considered and rejected because the intermediate and root computations serve different roles and have different inputs: intermediate binding is independent of the message, whereas root binding commits to it.

===Message-Independent Intermediate Aggregation===

The message is deliberately omitted from ''NonceAggExt''. This allows nonce aggregation within nested subgroups before the message is determined. Only the root nonce-binding factor and the final BIP340 challenge commit to the message. Including the message in intermediate binding would unnecessarily make every nested subgroup's first-round output message-specific and would remove this preprocessing property without being required by the referenced construction.

===Retention of Internal Aggregate Nonces===

A nested signer requires the internal, pre-binding aggregate nonce of each aggregation node on its path in order to reconstruct the intermediate binding factors during partial signing. An external nonce is insufficient because it already contains the binding transformation applied by ''NonceAggExt''. For this reason, every signing path carries the sequence ''(out<sub>0</sub>, ..., out<sub>Λ−1</sub>)''. The specification does not require a particular protocol for transporting these values. Implementations may store them directly or reconstruct them from authenticated or otherwise integrity-protected first-round transcript state.

===Path-Local Session Context===

A leaf signer is not required to know the complete nested signer tree.

At every aggregation level on its own path, the signer needs:
* the public key by which it is represented at that level;
* the other participant public keys at that level; and
* the internal aggregate nonce for that level.

These values are sufficient to reconstruct the key-aggregation and nonce-binding coefficients on the signer's path. A subtree that is not expanded on the signer's path can therefore be represented solely by its 33-byte aggregate plain public key. This preserves the abstraction boundary provided by nested aggregation and avoids requiring unrelated participants to learn the internal participant structure of other nested groups.

===Accumulated Coefficients===

A leaf's contribution to the root aggregate key is multiplied by one BIP327 key-aggregation coefficient at every aggregation level on its path. Similarly, its second nonce contribution is transformed by one nonce-binding factor at every relevant level. Consequently, leaf signing uses the accumulated values ''b̌ = b<sub>0</sub>·...·b<sub>Λ−1</sub> mod n'' and ''č = c·a<sub>0</sub>·...·a<sub>Λ−1</sub> mod n''. These products are how the recursive tree collapses into a single root Schnorr verification equation. A nested subgroup has no separate aggregate secret signing key. Instead, its second-round contribution is the scalar sum of its descendants' contributions.

===Intermediate Partial-Signature Aggregation===

Intermediate partial-signature aggregation consists only of scalar addition. No additional tweak term is introduced at a non-root node. Under the restrictions of this specification, intermediate aggregate keys are untweaked, and the required recursive key and nonce coefficients have already been incorporated into the descendants' partial signatures.

After intermediate aggregation, a nested subgroup is represented at its parent by exactly three protocol objects:
* its 33-byte aggregate plain public key;
* its 66-byte external nonce; and
* its 32-byte aggregate partial signature.

These objects satisfy the same form of partial-signature verification equation as a direct participant at the parent level.

===Root-Only Aggregate-Key Tweaking===

The referenced Nested MuSig2 construction does not itself specify BIP327 aggregate-key tweaking. This specification permits BIP327 ''ApplyTweak'' only at the root because BIP327 already defines how root tweak parity and the accumulated tweak scalar are incorporated into signing and final signature aggregation. Allowing ''ApplyTweak'' at an intermediate node would introduce additional parity and additive tweak terms into the recursive relation between descendant partial signatures and the public key presented to the parent. The algorithms in this specification do not account for those terms. This BIP therefore does not define intermediate tweaking. This restriction does not imply that an extension supporting such tweaks is impossible; such an extension would require additional algorithms and separate security analysis.

===Root Signature Aggregation===

Final root aggregation uses BIP327 ''PartialSigAgg'' unchanged.

By the time contributions reach the root, every nested subtree is represented in the same forms expected for an ordinary BIP327 participant. Reusing the BIP327 root algorithm ensures that:
* root aggregate-key tweaks are applied according to BIP327;
* the ordinary <code>MuSig/noncecoef</code> root binding is used;
* BIP327 effective-nonce parity and point-at-infinity rules are retained;
* the root tweak contribution is added exactly once; and
* the final output has the ordinary 64-byte BIP340 signature encoding.

No NestedMuSig2-specific object is exposed to the final BIP340 verifier.

==Backward Compatibility==

NestedMuSig2 does not introduce a new Bitcoin signature type, public-key encoding, transaction witness format, or consensus validation rule. The final output of a successful NestedMuSig2 signing session is an ordinary 64-byte BIP340 Schnorr signature under an ordinary 32-byte BIP340 X-only public key. A BIP340 verifier does not receive, and does not need to know, the nested signer tree, intermediate aggregate keys, internal aggregate nonces, external nonces, or partial signatures. Consequently, software that only verifies the completed BIP340 signature does not require NestedMuSig2 support.

===Bitcoin Consensus and Taproot===

NestedMuSig2 is an off-chain signing protocol. It requires no consensus change, soft fork, or new script opcode. When the resulting X-only aggregate public key is used in a context that already accepts BIP340 signatures, the completed NestedMuSig2 signature is verified using the existing BIP340 verification algorithm.

In particular, when the root aggregate key is used as a Taproot output key, the blockchain does not reveal whether the signature was produced by:
* a single signer;
* an ordinary BIP327 MuSig2 signing group; or
* a NestedMuSig2 signing tree,

except to the extent that such information is revealed through other application or transaction metadata.

This specification does not modify BIP341 Taproot validation rules.

===Output Script Descriptors===

This specification does not define a new output script descriptor expression for representing NestedMuSig2 signer trees. At the time this BIP was written, BIP390 defines the <code>musig()</code> descriptor key expression for BIP327 aggregate keys, but explicitly prohibits nesting one <code>musig()</code> expression inside another. Consequently, a NestedMuSig2 tree cannot be represented directly by nesting the existing BIP390 syntax, for example: <code>musig(KEY_A, musig(KEY_B, KEY_C))</code> is not a valid BIP390 expression. An existing descriptor may contain the already-computed aggregate public key of a nested subgroup where an ordinary key expression is permitted, but doing so does not encode the subgroup's internal signing structure and is therefore insufficient by itself for wallet recovery or coordination of NestedMuSig2 signing. A descriptor representation for nested signer trees, if desired, requires a separate specification or an extension of the applicable descriptor standard. Such descriptor syntax is outside the scope of this BIP.

===Wallet and Protocol Compatibility===

Wallets, hardware signers, remote signers, and coordinator protocols that understand only BIP327 MUST NOT assume that they can participate internally in a NestedMuSig2 subtree without additional support.

NestedMuSig2-aware software must additionally understand at least:
* recursive public-key aggregation;
* the distinction between internal and external aggregate nonces;
* ''NonceAggExt'';
* path-local Session Contexts;
* accumulated key and nonce coefficients; and
* intermediate partial-signature aggregation.

Applications must also coordinate the nested first- and second-round message flow required to move aggregate contributions between child and parent aggregation nodes. No particular wallet, hardware-signing, PSBT, descriptor, or transport protocol integration is defined by this BIP unless explicitly stated elsewhere.

===ECDSA Compatibility===

Like BIP327, NestedMuSig2 produces BIP340 Schnorr signatures and does not produce ECDSA signatures. Existing Bitcoin applications or script contexts that require ECDSA cannot use a NestedMuSig2 signature without separately gaining support for a BIP340-compatible signing context.

===Version and Protocol Negotiation===

The internal NestedMuSig2 signing protocol is not interchangeable with an ordinary BIP327 session of the same participant keys when ''Λ > 1''. In particular, the intermediate tagged hash <code>NestedMuSig/aggnoncecoef</code>, external nonce transformation, path-dependent coefficients, and intermediate partial-signature aggregation are specific to this specification. Applications that exchange NestedMuSig2 protocol messages SHOULD therefore have an unambiguous way to determine that all parties responsible for nested processing are using the same version of this specification. This BIP does not mandate a particular transport-level negotiation mechanism.

===Nonce Generation===

The reference implementation MUST use BIP327 ''NonceGen'' semantics unchanged.

In particular, leaf nonce generation uses:
* <code>MuSig/aux</code>; and
* <code>MuSig/nonce</code>.

The reference implementation MUST NOT substitute NestedMuSig2-specific tags for these operations. For deterministic test-vector generation, the implementation MAY expose an internal helper that accepts a caller-supplied 32-byte <code>rand'</code> value. Such a helper exists only to make test vectors reproducible. The ordinary nonce-generation entry point used to model real protocol behavior MUST obtain <code>rand'</code> from a cryptographically secure random number generator as required by BIP327.

===Intermediate Nonce Binding===

The reference implementation of ''NonceAggExt'' MUST compute ''b = int(hash<sub>NestedMuSig/aggnoncecoef</sub>(pk_agg || aggnonce)) mod n''.

Here:
* ''pk_agg'' is exactly the 33-byte BIP327 plain aggregate public key; and
* ''aggnonce'' is exactly the 66-byte internal aggregate nonce.

The implementation MUST NOT replace ''pk_agg'' by an X-only public-key encoding and MUST NOT include the message in this computation. If either resulting external nonce component is the point at infinity, ''NonceAggExt'' MUST fail rather than serializing the component using ''cbytes_ext''. Every successful ''NonceAggExt'' output therefore consists of two ordinary finite compressed secp256k1 points and can be consumed by the parent's unchanged BIP327 ''NonceAgg'' algorithm.

===Session and Signing State===

The reference Session Context represents ''(nonce_path, cosigner_key_path, tweaks, is_xonly_t, m)''. All Session Context fields are public. Secret nonce state is separate from the Session Context and MUST be treated as single-use. The reference implementation SHOULD model consumption explicitly, for example by using a mutable object whose nonce scalars are erased or marked unavailable when ''Sign'' begins. A call to ''Sign'' MUST consume its supplied secret nonce before performing any subsequent operation that can fail. A second invocation using the same secret-nonce state MUST fail. The reference implementation MAY copy secret-nonce values when required solely for deterministic tests, but such copies MUST be clearly marked as unsafe and MUST NOT be presented as an implementation pattern.

===Session-Value Computation===

''GetSessionValues'' SHOULD expose or make testable the intermediate values required by the NestedMuSig2 test vectors, including:
* reconstructed ''pk<sub>d</sub>'' values;
* sorted ''L<sub>d</sub>'' lists;
* key-aggregation coefficients ''a<sub>d</sub>'';
* intermediate binding factors ''b<sub>d</sub>'';
* root binding factor ''b<sub>0</sub>'';
* final root key ''Q'';
* ''gacc'' and ''tacc'';
* effective nonce ''R'';
* ordinary BIP340 challenge ''c'';
* accumulated binding coefficient ''b̌''; and
* accumulated challenge coefficient ''č''.

The implementation MUST retain ''c'' and ''č'' as distinct values. The former is required for final root tweak aggregation, while the latter is used for recursive partial signing and partial-signature verification.

===Partial Signatures===

The reference ''Sign'' function returns only the 32-byte partial signature specified by this BIP. ''PartialSigVerify'' accepts one participant public nonce, one participant plain public key, one partial signature, and the Session Context corresponding to that participant's position. This specification does not require a separate nested ''PartialSigVerifyInternal'' API. ''PartialSigAggIntermediate'' implements intermediate subgroup aggregation and performs the scalar aggregation defined above. At the root, the reference implementation MUST use the BIP327 final partial-signature aggregation computation, including the root tweak contribution, without adding any additional NestedMuSig2-specific scalar term.

===BIP340 Verification===

The reference implementation MUST verify every successful end-to-end test vector using ordinary BIP340 verification. The BIP340 verification helper MUST accept messages according to the current BIP340 message semantics and MUST NOT impose a 32-byte-only message restriction.

Final verification MUST receive only:
* the final 32-byte X-only root public key;
* the message; and
* the final 64-byte signature.

It MUST NOT depend on any NestedMuSig2-specific signing state.

===Testing===

Running the reference implementation's test suite MUST execute all NestedMuSig2 test-vector suites defined by this specification. Tests that are temporarily disabled during development MUST NOT remain disabled in the version published with the BIP.

The test suite MUST include checks that:
* unchanged BIP327 primitives continue to satisfy their BIP327 vectors;
* NestedMuSig2-specific vectors produce the expected intermediate values;
* partial signatures verify at both leaf and nested-subgroup boundaries;
* intermediate aggregate contributions verify using truncated Session Contexts;
* secret nonces cannot be reused;
* root aggregation produces the expected signature; and
* every successful final signature passes ordinary BIP340 verification.

Implementers are encouraged to reproduce the test vectors independently rather than treating the Python implementation as an independent proof of the specification.

==Security Considerations==

NestedMuSig2 is an interactive multi-signature protocol. Its security depends on correct nonce handling, correct recursive computation of key and nonce coefficients, consistent session state, and faithful implementation of the algorithms specified in this document. The security considerations of BIP327 apply in addition to the NestedMuSig2-specific considerations described below.

===Security Model and Number of Nonces===

The Nested MuSig2 paper provides security reductions for variants of the recursive construction under the Algebraic One-More Discrete Logarithm (AOMDL) assumption. The paper gives security results under different modeling assumptions depending on the nonce construction. In particular, the practically relevant compact construction uses two nonce points per signer and is analyzed in the random-oracle model together with the algebraic group model (ROM+AGM). This specification fixes ''ν = 2'' in order to remain compatible with BIP327, whose participant public nonce consists of exactly two elliptic-curve points. Accordingly, the two-nonce NestedMuSig2 construction specified by this BIP corresponds to the paper's compact ROM+AGM security result. It MUST NOT be described as being covered by the paper's ROM-only security theorem without also stating the additional assumptions required for the two-nonce instantiation.

This specification additionally makes concrete interoperability choices not defined by the abstract construction in the paper, including:
* BIP327 optimized key aggregation;
* mandatory ''KeySort'' at each aggregation node;
* concrete secp256k1 point encodings;
* concrete tagged-hash domain strings;
* exceptional-point handling; and
* BIP327 aggregate-key tweaking at the root.

The paper's security proof motivates the recursive construction, but it MUST NOT be interpreted as an independent proof of every additional Bitcoin-specific convention introduced by this BIP.

===Secret Nonce Reuse===

A secret nonce MUST NOT be used in more than one invocation of ''Sign''.

Nonce reuse can disclose the signer's secret key. This requirement applies even if:
* the messages differ;
* the aggregate public keys differ;
* the signing trees differ;
* the signer occupies a different nesting position;
* one signing attempt subsequently fails;
* one session is NestedMuSig2 and another is ordinary BIP327 MuSig2; or
* the nonce is reused only a small number of times.

A ''secnonce'' supplied to ''Sign'' MUST therefore be considered permanently consumed when that invocation begins, regardless of whether the invocation later succeeds. Implementations SHOULD use opaque, consuming secret-nonce objects or equivalent state-management mechanisms that prevent accidental reuse. Where practical, secret nonce scalars SHOULD be securely erased after consumption. Retrying ''Sign'' with the same secret nonce after a parsing, network, coordinator, or Session Context failure is unsafe.

===Nonce Generation===

BIP327 ''NonceGen'' is used unchanged and its security requirements apply. In particular, the internal value <code>rand'</code> MUST be a fresh, unbiased, uniformly random 32-byte value obtained from a cryptographically secure random number generator.

The nonce scalars MUST NOT be generated deterministically solely from:
* the message;
* public keys;
* the signer tree;
* aggregate nonces; or
* other session parameters controlled or influenced by an adversary.

The optional ''sk'', ''aggpk'', ''m'', and ''extra_in'' inputs provide defense in depth if randomness is accidentally repeated, but they do not replace the requirement for high-quality randomness. Applications that generate nonces before the message or complete signing policy is known retain less defense-in-depth information in ''NonceGen'' and must be especially careful to prevent reuse of stored nonce state. This specification does not define NestedMuSig2 variants of BIP327 ''CounterNonceGen'' or ''DeterministicSign''. Their security properties MUST NOT be assumed to carry over automatically to nested signing.

===Binding the Signing Key Before Nonce Publication===

The individual plain public key stored in ''secnonce'' MUST correspond to the secret key later supplied to ''Sign''. For a leaf signer, this key is the signer's individual 33-byte plain public key. It is not an intermediate subgroup key or the root aggregate key. The public-key binding inherited from BIP327 ensures that the secret signing key is fixed before the corresponding public nonce is revealed. Removing this check can permit attacks in which an adversary chooses between related signing keys after observing nonce information. Leaf keys MAY be derived or tweaked before ''NonceGen'' is invoked. The final individual key pair that ''Sign'' will use, however, MUST already be determined when its public nonce is generated.

===Rogue-Key Resistance===

Every aggregation node MUST use the BIP327 ''KeyAgg'' construction, including its key-aggregation coefficients. A node MUST NOT replace ''KeyAgg'' with simple elliptic-curve point addition. The key-aggregation coefficients provide MuSig-style protection against rogue-key attacks. The same protection is required independently at every level of a NestedMuSig2 tree. After a child node computes its BIP327 aggregate public key, its parent treats the resulting 33-byte plain public key as a single participant key. The parent does not need to know the participant keys inside the child subtree.

===Recursive Nonce Binding===

The intermediate nonce-binding transformation performed by ''NonceAggExt'' is security-critical. For every non-root aggregation node, the intermediate binding factor is derived from that node's aggregate plain public key and its internal aggregate nonce. The factor transforms the second aggregate nonce component before the node appears as a participant to its parent. A signer then accumulates the binding factors along its path: ''b̌ = b<sub>0</sub>·b<sub>1</sub>·...·b<sub>Λ−1</sub> mod n''.

Implementations MUST NOT:
* omit an intermediate binding factor;
* substitute an external nonce for the corresponding internal aggregate nonce;
* use the wrong intermediate aggregate public key;
* change the order or serialization of the tagged-hash inputs;
* include the message in an intermediate binding factor;
* replace the intermediate tagged hash by the root tagged hash; or
* apply a binding factor at the wrong aggregation level.

Such modifications change the recursive signing equation and are not covered by this specification's security argument. The intermediate and root nonce-binding domains MUST remain distinct.

===Internal and External Aggregate Nonces===

Internal and external aggregate nonces are different protocol objects. An internal aggregate nonce ''out<sub>d</sub>'' is the output of ''NonceAgg'' before the node's intermediate binding factor is applied. An external nonce is the output of ''NonceAggExt'' and is the public nonce by which a nested node is represented at its parent. The internal aggregate nonce is required during signing to reconstruct ''b<sub>d</sub>''. Therefore, an external nonce MUST NOT be substituted for an internal nonce in ''nonce_path''. Implementations SHOULD use distinct types or otherwise clearly distinguish internal aggregate nonces from parent-facing external nonces.

===Session Consistency===

A partial signature is valid only for one exact signing session.

A leaf's signing computation depends on:
* every cosigner-key multiset on its path;
* every internal aggregate nonce on its path;
* the root aggregate-key tweak sequence;
* the corresponding tweak modes;
* the resulting root aggregate public key; and
* the message.

Changing any of these values changes the signing equation. Cached values derived from "GetSessionValues" MUST be reused only with the exact Session Context from which they were derived. Implementations SHOULD treat an accepted Session Context as immutable and MUST protect it and derived cached values against unauthorized modification during signing. A signer MUST verify at the application layer that the message and signing policy correspond to the action it intends to authorize before releasing its partial signature. Cryptographic validity of a Session Context does not by itself establish user or application authorization.

===Malicious Aggregators===

An aggregator need not be trusted for unforgeability solely because it performs public aggregation computations. As with BIP327, an untrusted aggregator may nevertheless deliberately cause a signing session to abort.

A malicious NestedMuSig2 aggregator may disrupt a session by:
* omitting participant contributions;
* substituting or modifying contributions;
* distributing inconsistent aggregate nonces;
* distributing inconsistent Session Contexts;
* withholding required protocol messages;
* supplying malformed intermediate state; or
* refusing to complete aggregation.

NestedMuSig2 contains potentially several aggregation boundaries, so a malicious internal coordinator may disrupt a subtree even though its parent sees only the subgroup's aggregate public key, external nonce, and aggregate partial signature. Applications requiring blame attribution SHOULD preserve enough transcript information to associate participant occurrences with the public keys, nonces, partial signatures, and aggregate values they supplied.

===Identifiable Aborts===

''PartialSigVerify'' can identify some malformed or incorrect second-round contributions before final aggregation. However, partial-signature verification does not guarantee that every abort can be attributed to an individual leaf.

For example, the parent of a nested subgroup may know only:
* the subgroup's aggregate plain public key;
* the subgroup's external nonce; and
* the subgroup's aggregate partial signature.

If the subgroup's aggregate contribution fails verification, the parent may identify the subgroup as the failing participant but may not have the subgroup's internal transcript needed to identify a particular leaf. Applications requiring leaf-level or hierarchical blame SHOULD retain participant-level transcripts inside every relevant subgroup. Identifiable-abort guarantees also depend on honest parties agreeing on the transcript being verified. This BIP does not specify a transcript-consensus or transport-authentication protocol.

===Partial Signatures Are Not Proofs of Knowledge===

Successful ''PartialSigVerify'' MUST NOT be interpreted as proof that the participant knows a secret key corresponding to ''pk''. A MuSig2 partial signature is not a standalone Schnorr signature or a proof-of-possession protocol. Its purpose is to determine whether a contribution is consistent with the partial-signature equation for a particular signing session and, where possible, to identify disruptive contributions. Applications requiring proof of possession MUST use a separately specified mechanism.

===Duplicate Public Keys===

Duplicate participant public-key occurrences are permitted as in BIP327. Duplicate byte strings MUST NOT silently merge participant occurrences.

Each occurrence has its own:
* participant position;
* nonce contribution; and
* second-round contribution.

Applications MAY impose a policy that rejects duplicate public keys, for example where duplicate keys indicate configuration errors or a lack of independent key material. Such checks are application policy rather than a requirement of the NestedMuSig2 cryptographic construction.

===Aggregate-Key Tweaking===

This specification supports BIP327 aggregate-key tweaking only at the root. ''ApplyTweak'' MUST NOT be applied to intermediate aggregate keys. An intermediate tweak introduces additional parity and additive tweak terms into the recursive key relation. The signing and aggregation equations defined by this BIP do not account for those terms. The referenced Nested MuSig2 construction does not itself specify BIP327 aggregate-key tweaking. Root-only tweaking is therefore a concrete extension defined by this BIP and deserves separate implementation and cryptographic review.

Implementations supporting root tweaks SHOULD include interoperability tests covering:
* plain tweaks;
* X-only tweaks;
* multiple sequential tweaks;
* root parity changes; and
* final BIP340 verification.

===Point-at-Infinity Handling===

Exceptional-point behavior MUST be implemented exactly as specified. Internal aggregate nonce components may be the point at infinity and are encoded using BIP327 ''cbytes_ext''. External nonce components, however, are consumed by the parent's BIP327 ''NonceAgg'' as participant nonce points and MUST therefore must not be infinite or ''G''.

Consequently:
* ''NonceAggExt'' MUST fail if an external nonce component would be infinity;
* an intermediate binding scalar equal to zero MUST NOT be replaced by another scalar;
* an infinite external component MUST NOT be replaced by ''G'' or another point; and
* only root effective-nonce processing applies BIP327's rule that substitutes ''G'' if the final effective aggregate nonce is infinity.

Although these events occur only with negligible probability for honestly generated values, malformed attacker-controlled inputs MUST be handled without crashes, assertion failures, memory-safety violations, or undefined behavior.

===Privacy of Nested Structure===

At the cryptographic interface between a nested subgroup and its parent, the subgroup is represented by:
* one aggregate plain public key;
* one external nonce; and
* one aggregate partial signature.

The NestedMuSig2 construction is designed so that a parent need not learn whether such a participant is an individual signer or another nested signing group. This property does not imply complete application-level anonymity or unlinkability.

The nested structure may still be revealed through:
* network connections;
* protocol timing;
* participant identities;
* coordinator metadata;
* descriptor or wallet state;
* logs and audit records;
* persistent reuse of aggregate keys;
* observable failures; or
* explicit disclosure by participants.

Applications requiring subgroup privacy must therefore consider transport and metadata leakage separately from the cryptographic signing protocol.

===Availability and Denial of Service===

NestedMuSig2 remains an ''n''-of-''n'' protocol at every aggregation node. Every required participant in every required subtree must participate in order for the root signature to complete. Any required signer or aggregator can therefore prevent successful signing by refusing to participate or by supplying invalid contributions. Nesting does not provide ''t''-of-''n'' threshold signing, redundancy, or fault tolerance. Applications requiring threshold availability require a threshold-signature scheme or another policy mechanism.

Large or deeply nested trees can also consume substantial public-state, hashing, and elliptic-curve computation resources. Implementations processing untrusted signing descriptions SHOULD apply application-appropriate limits to:
* nesting depth;
* number of participants per node;
* total number of participant occurrences;
* Session Context size; and
* message and transcript sizes.

===Transport and Transcript Security===

This BIP does not define a network transport protocol. Applications must ensure that received protocol values are associated with the intended signing session and, where necessary, with the participant or aggregator that supplied them.

Depending on the application threat model, suitable mechanisms may include:
* unique session identifiers;
* authenticated communication channels;
* signed protocol messages;
* authenticated transcripts; or
* persistent audit records.

This BIP is out of scope for such mechanisms.

===Side Channels and Secret Memory===

The accompanying Python reference implementation is not suitable for production use. Production implementations SHOULD use constant-time cryptographic operations for computations involving secret scalars and MUST avoid implementation behavior that exposes secret keys or secret nonce material through avoidable side channels.

Implementations SHOULD minimize unnecessary copies of:
* secret signing keys;
* secret nonce scalars; and
* secret intermediate scalar values.

Where reliable immediate memory erasure is unavailable, implementations should nevertheless structure ownership of secret nonce state so that consumed nonce material cannot be reused.

===Final Signature Verification===

A successful NestedMuSig2 signing session produces an ordinary BIP340 signature. Implementations SHOULD verify the completed signature using ordinary BIP340 verification before releasing, broadcasting, or otherwise relying on it.

Final verification requires only:
* the final 32-byte X-only root public key;
* the message; and
* the final 64-byte BIP340 signature.

The final verifier does not require knowledge of the signer tree, intermediate aggregate keys, nonce path, partial signatures, or any other NestedMuSig2 state.

